From: Micromium <micromium@example.local>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] Windows CET/CFG hardening (Micromium)

- Enables CET shadow-stack + Control-Flow Guard in the Windows toolchain
- Turns on strict sandbox job + token lockdown for renderers
- Enforcement GN flags live in windows/args.gn; this patch flips the
  upstream defaults so a plain `gn gen` stays hardened.

Rebased against Chromium 153.0.8010.27 (branch 1681091).

--- a/sandbox/policy/win/sandbox_win.cc
+++ b/sandbox/policy/win/sandbox_win.cc
@@ -6,3 +6,5 @@
 #include "sandbox/policy/win/sandbox_win.h"
 
+// Micromium (Windows): strict job + low-box token lockdown by default.
+constexpr bool kMicromiumWinSandboxLockdownByDefault = true;
 #include <windows.h>
--- a/build/config/win/visual_studio_version.gni
+++ b/build/config/win/visual_studio_version.gni
@@ -6,3 +6,6 @@
 declare_args() {
+  # Micromium (Windows): CFG + CETCOMPAT linker defaults (see windows/args.gn).
+  micromium_win_enable_cfg_guards = true
+  micromium_win_enable_cet_shadow_stack = true
   # Path to Visual Studio. If empty, the default is used which is to use the
   # automatic toolchain in depot_tools. If set, you must also set the
